    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of everything that happens for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. Every step runs under one `transaction` governance, so all the writes commit once at the very end.\n\n## 0. Endpoint guard (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is rejected (\u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n## 1. Bean-validation of the request body\n`BuildOwner` binds `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, so the DTO constraints run first; any failure is a 400 via the `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler:\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, with up to two space/`'`/`-` separated parts)\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, allowing a trailing `.`)\n- `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n- `postcode` \u2014 if present, `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n- `registrationDate` / `birthDate` \u2014 valid ISO `LocalDate` if present\n\n## 2. `BuildOwner` (build step) \u2014 internal order\n1. **Normalize address** (side-effect): trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE` abbreviations.\n2. **Required-field check** (validation): `firstName`, `lastName`, normalized `address` (non-empty *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone` \u2014 any blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (carries the list of missing fields).\n3. **Normalize telephone** to E.164 (side-effect) \u2014 strips separators, applies default country code `+61`, drops a leading `0`, enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length; invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n4. **Store normalized address** back on the request (side-effect).\n5. **Normalize email** (validation + side-effect): if present, trim, require syntactic validity \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` if malformed, else store lower-cased (absent stays null).\n6. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (side-effect).\n7. **Registration date resolution** (validation + side-effect): default to server date when omitted; if a supplied date is after today \u2192 `RegistrationDateInFutureException`; then roll a Saturday/Sunday forward to the next Monday (\"business day\") and store it.\n8. **Compute `customerCode`** (side-effect): `<REGION>-<HASH8>` derived from postcode/city region + SHA-256 of telephone+lastName.\n9. Publish the built `Owner` and the `sharesHousehold` boolean for later steps.\n\n## 3. `CheckOwnerEmailDomain` (validation)\nIf email present, reject disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n## 4. `CheckOwnerPostcode` (validation)\nIf postcode present, re-check 4-digit format and enforce the region range from the city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent = no-op.\n\n## 5. `AssignOwnerHousehold` (side-effect)\nCompute deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256 over normalized lastName + postcode) and stamp it; count and stamp `householdSize` (this owner + existing members with the same id). No rejection here.\n\n## 6. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (validation)\nUnless `sharesHousehold` is true, reject if any existing owner has the same `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409 Conflict).\n\n## 7. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` (validation)\nReject if the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409 Conflict).\n\n## 8. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` (validation)\nReject if \u2265 100 existing owners already share the (business-day-adjusted) registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429 Too Many Requests).\n\n## 9. `CheckOwnerBulkSignup` (side-effect)\nSet `bulkSignupWarning = true` when more than 80 existing owners share that registration date (no rejection).\n\n## 10. `CountOwnerNamesakes` (side-effect)\nCount existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive) and stamp `namesakeCount`.\n\n## 11. `CheckOwnerPossibleDuplicate` (side-effect)\nSkipped when `sharesHousehold` is true or no postcode. Otherwise, if an existing owner shares lastName + postcode but has a different telephone, mark `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf =` that owner's id (lowest id wins). No rejection.\n\n## 12. `SaveOwner` (side-effect)\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the entity and assigns its id.\n\n## 13. `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect)\nWrite one line to the `AUDIT` logger with the new owner's id, customerCode, registrationDate and derived membershipLevel.\n\n## 14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (response)\nMap `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` (deriving displayName, initials, checkDigit, membershipNumber/points/level, locality, contactPreference, identityKey, ageBand, telephoneDisplay) and send **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n---\n\n**Summary of the two categories, in order:**\n\n- **Validations (reject):** role guard \u2192 DTO bean-validation (400) \u2192 required fields (Missing) \u2192 telephone (Invalid) \u2192 email syntax (Invalid) \u2192 future registration date \u2192 disposable email domain \u2192 postcode region \u2192 household duplicate (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429).\n- **Side-effects (mutate/derive/persist):** address normalize \u2192 telephone normalize \u2192 email lower-case \u2192 entity map \u2192 registration-date default+business-day roll \u2192 customerCode \u2192 householdId + householdSize \u2192 bulkSignupWarning \u2192 namesakeCount \u2192 possibleDuplicate flags \u2192 **save (id assigned)** \u2192 audit log \u2192 201 response with derived DTO + Location header.\n\nNote the ordering consequence baked into `BuildOwner`: required-field and telephone/email checks happen inside the first step, but the semantic checks (domain, postcode region, duplicate, capacity, limit) run only after the entity is built \u2014 all within a single transaction that commits after the responder."
